A release that gives a lender time but leaves the borrowers it lends to where they waited,
since it looks for borrowers only of threads on a queue, which a lender never is.
The borrower waits on another queue than its lender's account says.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a place waits on another queue than its account says
Witness: fuzz lend-lender-earns

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -844,3 +844,3 @@ static void release(uint32_t c)
         const struct thread *x = place_thread(p);
-        for (uint32_t d = 0; d < LEND_DEPTH && x->lend_to != 0; d++) {
+        for (uint32_t d = 0; d < LEND_DEPTH && x->lend_to != 0 && p->queue != QUEUE_NONE; d++) {
             LOOP_BOUND(LEND_DEPTH);
